<title>USA: Kopin Corp Q1 net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Kopin Corp Q1 net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>TAUNTON, Mass. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					Mar 29, 1997	 Mar 30, 1996</p>
<p> Total revenue			 4,028,910	    5,333,634</p>
<p>  Non-recurring impairment charge	  -	    4,990,412</p>
<p>Loss before minority interest</p>
<p>					 (2,101,618)	  (9,278,299)</p>
<p>Minority interest in loss</p>
<p>   of subsidiary				 -		557,246</p>
<p> Net loss			   ( 2,101,618)    ( 8,721,053)(a)</p>
<p>Net loss per weighted average  </p>
<p> number of common shares	     ( 0.19)		( 0.80)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  common shares outstanding     10,940,988	   10,915,858</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net loss for the first quarter of 1996 includes write-down of certain intangible and long-lived assets in connection with the company's adoption of the provisions of Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 121, as well as certain non-recurring research and development charges, totaling $5.5 million, or $0.50 per share.</p>
<p>The company said the decline in revenue for the first quarter of 1997 compared to 1996 primarily relates to its write-off of its investment in a majority owned subsidiary, Forte Technologies Inc as of December 31, 1996.  The subsidiary had sales of approximately $1,400,000 in the first quarter of 1996.  Forte's 1997 financial results are no longer consolidated with Kopin's as they were in 1996.</p>
</text>
